      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "IDEAL MOTH (1) has been unplaced from this barrier in her last two outings but took on some good mares last week so will enjoy a class drop. Came from a wider barrier to score three back at this circuit and distance. Could show her best in this line-up. RED SAPPHIRE (3) returns to the city with his hoof on the till after placing in his last three outings. Led and stuck on when beaten 1.2m in this grade at Newcastle last start so can take advantage of another good draw. Former Kiwi HUNGRY BRONNIE NZ (2) made a winning start for Brad Hewitt when defeating some smart rivals at Wagga last start. Rises in grade and tackles the boys here but she draws well and has upside. WITHDISTINCTION (10) and CYA ART NZ (7) may require some luck from their draws but are both good enough with their A-games.",
